  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Stable release with breaking changes from 1.0.2.\n\t\t- Strict 1-to-1 WinAPI naming: All structs, handles, and enums now strictly match native C headers.\n\t\t- Handle Localization: Handles are now strongly typed and moved to their origin namespaces (e.g., ProcessHandle in Kernel32, TokenHandle in Advapi32, HDC in GDI32).\n\t\t- Extended API Coverage: Expanded imports for Shell32, User32, MSimg32, and SHCore.\n\t\t- Zero-Cost Safety: Replaced raw pointers with strict ref/in/out modifiers for non-nullable arguments. Fixed struct ABI layout bugs.",
